# xsec_mg5.mg5 -- the hard-photon cross section e- e+ -> mu- mu+ gamma with the SpinorQED UFO (research note models/spinor_qed,
# step (6)).  Run from Src/:   mg5_aMC xsec_mg5.mg5 > work/xsec_mg5.log   (run_xsec_check.sh does this)
# Imports a copy of generated/SpinorQED_UFO in work/ (MadGraph converts UFOs to Python 3 in place).
# Fixed-energy beams (lpp = 0) in the CM frame, e- along +z (beam 1), param_card defaults m_e = 1, m_mu = 1.7, e = 1.
# All default cuts on leptons and photons are switched off (ptl, etal, drll, pta, etaa, draa, dral) and the photon energy is
# cut at E_gamma > 0.1 (ea; the CM frame), the soft-hard boundary DeltaE of the note.  sqrt(s) = 4, 6, 10 in this order
# (xsec_numeric.py relies on it), 50000 unweighted events each (the forward-backward asymmetry is counted from the LHE files).
# Then two diagnostic runs (20000 events): sqrt(s) = 6 and 10 with the photon kept away from the beams, |cos theta_gamma| < 0.9
# (etaa = atanh(0.9)), and sqrt(s) = 6 without that cut but with sde_strategy 2.  Then the standalone matrix element
# (work/sa_xsec3, evaluated at fixed points with tree_me_points.f).
set automatic_html_opening False
import model ./work/SpinorQED_UFO
generate e- e+ > mu- mu+ a
output work/mg5_xsec3 -f
launch work/mg5_xsec3
0
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set nevents 50000
set ptl 0
set etal -1
set drll 0
set pta 0
set etaa -1
set draa 0
set dral 0
set ea 0.1
set ebeam1 2.0
set ebeam2 2.0
0
launch work/mg5_xsec3
0
set ebeam1 3.0
set ebeam2 3.0
0
launch work/mg5_xsec3
0
set ebeam1 5.0
set ebeam2 5.0
0
launch work/mg5_xsec3
0
set nevents 20000
set ebeam1 3.0
set ebeam2 3.0
set etaa 1.4722194895832204
0
launch work/mg5_xsec3
0
set ebeam1 5.0
set ebeam2 5.0
0
launch work/mg5_xsec3
0
set ebeam1 3.0
set ebeam2 3.0
set etaa -1
set sde_strategy 2
0
output standalone work/sa_xsec3 -f
